1
00:00:02,632 --> 00:00:08,859
[SPEAKER_00]: So, a couple of suttas, maybe, on a similar theme.

2
00:00:12,936 --> 00:00:20,420
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the sangita nikāya, the saḷāyatana, the senses.

3
00:00:22,501 --> 00:00:23,241
[SPEAKER_00]: 153.

4
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:28,203
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, there is a method...

5
00:00:28,424 --> 00:00:30,665
[SPEAKER_00]: Sorry, no, he asks the monks.

6
00:00:31,085 --> 00:00:41,410
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, is there a method by means of which bhikkhu, from a place other than faith, other than preference, other than tradition,

7
00:00:43,007 --> 00:00:52,064
[SPEAKER_00]: Other than an examination of properties, other than relying upon the insight from a view,

8
00:00:54,073 --> 00:00:56,075
[SPEAKER_01]: Just examination of the properties.

9
00:00:56,195 --> 00:00:56,415
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

10
00:00:56,856 --> 00:00:58,437
[SPEAKER_00]: That's basically psychologizing.

11
00:00:58,798 --> 00:00:59,338
[SPEAKER_00]: It is, isn't it?

12
00:00:59,558 --> 00:01:02,762
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how I... basically, it's hard to translate these terms.

13
00:01:02,842 --> 00:01:03,202
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

14
00:01:03,222 --> 00:01:10,729
[SPEAKER_01]: So, but I sort of was thinking about... Yeah, it's exactly like... just examining... just informing yourself about the properties, observing the properties of the thing.

15
00:01:10,849 --> 00:01:11,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

16
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:13,472
[SPEAKER_01]: You mistake for understanding the nature of the thing.

17
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:13,732
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

18
00:01:13,752 --> 00:01:16,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is the nature of, basically, the core of psychology.

19
00:01:16,495 --> 00:01:16,895
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

20
00:01:17,296 --> 00:01:18,377
[SPEAKER_00]: It's akāra.

21
00:01:19,217 --> 00:01:20,437
[SPEAKER_00]: Parivrttika.

22
00:01:20,457 --> 00:01:25,438
[SPEAKER_00]: So, like, thinking about the akhāra, which could be the... what makes the thing.

23
00:01:25,599 --> 00:01:26,979
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, what it's made of.

24
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:27,759
[SPEAKER_00]: What it's made of.

25
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:28,359
[SPEAKER_00]: Properties.

26
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:28,839
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

27
00:01:28,859 --> 00:01:29,939
[SPEAKER_00]: Its qualities, or...

28
00:01:29,959 --> 00:01:32,220
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

29
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,020
[SPEAKER_00]: Its components.

30
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:33,840
[SPEAKER_00]: Its components.

31
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

32
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:36,321
[SPEAKER_00]: Analysis, for the sake of it.

33
00:01:36,441 --> 00:01:36,681
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

34
00:01:38,901 --> 00:01:41,682
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh... Where are we?

35
00:01:46,974 --> 00:01:55,402
[SPEAKER_00]: So, from a place other than those, is there a method by means of which a bhikkhu might describe final knowledge?

36
00:01:55,722 --> 00:02:02,148
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, I understand that birth is destroyed, the whole life has been lived, what should be done has been done, there's no more of this.

37
00:02:03,069 --> 00:02:06,472
[SPEAKER_00]: And the bhikkhus say, I don't know, you tell us.

38
00:02:07,473 --> 00:02:08,935
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha says, yes, there is.

39
00:02:10,785 --> 00:02:25,091
[SPEAKER_00]: He then says, and which bhikkhus is the method by means of which a bhikkhu from a place other than faith, so on, might describe final knowledge, thus, I understand, but has destroyed, and so on.

40
00:02:26,612 --> 00:02:37,377
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he says, here, bhikkhus, a bhikkhu, having seen a sight with the eye, when there is passion, aversion, distraction internally,

41
00:02:38,578 --> 00:02:39,339
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

42
00:02:40,339 --> 00:02:48,706
[SPEAKER_00]: For me, there is passion, aversion, distraction internally.

43
00:02:48,746 --> 00:02:52,488
[SPEAKER_00]: That passion, aversion, distraction is just a compound word.

44
00:02:52,628 --> 00:02:53,149
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not...

45
00:02:53,849 --> 00:02:54,990
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not these different things.

46
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:55,931
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not these different things.

47
00:02:55,951 --> 00:03:02,316
[SPEAKER_00]: He just says passion, aversion, distraction, ragga, dosa, moha.

48
00:03:02,496 --> 00:03:04,697
[SPEAKER_01]: Basis of unwholesome.

49
00:03:04,717 --> 00:03:04,958
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

50
00:03:05,138 --> 00:03:07,119
[SPEAKER_00]: In another place, like the roots of the unwholesome.

51
00:03:07,139 --> 00:03:07,279
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

52
00:03:09,483 --> 00:03:12,044
[SPEAKER_00]: That's Madhyamini 9, where he says the roots to unwholesome.

53
00:03:12,064 --> 00:03:13,924
[SPEAKER_00]: So, so having seen...

54
00:03:15,545 --> 00:03:22,927
[SPEAKER_00]: When there is passion, aversion, distraction internally, he understands, for me, there is passion, aversion, distraction internally.

55
00:03:23,927 --> 00:03:28,708
[SPEAKER_00]: When there isn't passion, aversion, distraction internally, he understands, for me, there isn't.

56
00:03:28,788 --> 00:03:29,549
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

57
00:03:29,629 --> 00:03:32,349
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands there isn't this internally.

58
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:33,930
[SPEAKER_01]: He's clear about it.

59
00:03:34,744 --> 00:03:42,453
[SPEAKER_01]: And by the way, when we speak, when you say the necessary basis for things, that's what a root is.

60
00:03:43,174 --> 00:03:45,857
[SPEAKER_01]: A root is a necessary basis for the existence of a tree.

61
00:03:46,098 --> 00:03:48,561
[SPEAKER_01]: The root doesn't disappear once the trunk starts to grow.

62
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,623
[SPEAKER_01]: It needs to be there throughout.

63
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,762
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can have the trunk disappear, not the root necessarily.

64
00:03:55,123 --> 00:03:57,764
[SPEAKER_01]: But if the root disappears, the trunk cannot remain living.

65
00:03:58,365 --> 00:03:59,606
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the root of the unwholesome...

66
00:03:59,626 --> 00:04:02,728
[SPEAKER_00]: The root of the unwholesome is a necessary basis for unwholesome, yeah.

67
00:04:03,909 --> 00:04:06,931
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whenever you read about the root in the sutta, that's what it means.

68
00:04:06,971 --> 00:04:08,132
[SPEAKER_01]: Necessary basis for this.

69
00:04:09,033 --> 00:04:13,596
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding the necessary basis for greed and lust.

70
00:04:13,636 --> 00:04:15,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Necessary basis for aversion, for destruction.

71
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:30,242
[SPEAKER_01]: And you'll see probably later, I guess, but based on where that sutta is going, not understanding what necessary basis is, is what provides the necessary basis for these things.

72
00:04:30,302 --> 00:04:30,542
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

73
00:04:32,803 --> 00:04:39,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding the mind with greed, aversion, delusion, is already a step closer to overcoming the greed, aversion, delusion.

74
00:04:39,744 --> 00:04:39,924
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

75
00:04:40,545 --> 00:04:41,725
[SPEAKER_00]: It's simple, simply, once...

76
00:04:43,831 --> 00:04:55,357
[SPEAKER_00]: As paschal version destruction, if those... the necessary basis for wholesomeness is there, either you know it's there, or you don't.

77
00:04:55,397 --> 00:04:56,998
[SPEAKER_01]: And see, so that's the method.

78
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:58,039
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

79
00:04:58,359 --> 00:05:10,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Method is not to look in front of you, not to psychologize, not to be examining the properties, or just adhering to it blindly because the tradition told you so, or the authority of the teacher told you so.

80
00:05:10,986 --> 00:05:12,927
[SPEAKER_01]: The method is to discern the background,

81
00:05:13,858 --> 00:05:18,783
[SPEAKER_01]: Peripherally, what state of mind you are in, while this is happening to me in the front.

82
00:05:20,044 --> 00:05:23,928
[SPEAKER_01]: So, by seeing sight with the eye, instead of, hmm, what did I see?

83
00:05:23,988 --> 00:05:24,749
[SPEAKER_01]: What is it made of?

84
00:05:24,789 --> 00:05:25,570
[SPEAKER_01]: Where it came from?

85
00:05:25,610 --> 00:05:26,371
[SPEAKER_01]: How it came to be?

86
00:05:26,411 --> 00:05:27,332
[SPEAKER_01]: How does it affect me?

87
00:05:27,772 --> 00:05:28,833
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is in the front.

88
00:05:29,474 --> 00:05:36,361
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is rooted in you not seeing the state of mind simultaneously present with that sight, on account of that sight.

89
00:05:37,675 --> 00:05:43,480
[SPEAKER_01]: So, sure, yeah, there is a method which is completely opposite direction of any notion of method people might have.

90
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:47,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, usually, method is methodical analysis... Yeah, I mean, yeah.

91
00:05:47,202 --> 00:05:47,763
[SPEAKER_01]: ...performance.

92
00:05:48,143 --> 00:05:50,385
[SPEAKER_01]: But, no, as a word, method is absolutely fine.

93
00:05:50,405 --> 00:05:52,006
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just what people do on account of it.

94
00:05:52,026 --> 00:05:52,787
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know how to...

95
00:05:52,807 --> 00:05:53,807
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know how you talk about a way... Yeah.

96
00:05:53,828 --> 00:05:56,710
[SPEAKER_01]: No, there's nothing wrong with it, with a word in itself, with a term.

97
00:05:57,290 --> 00:05:57,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

98
00:05:57,550 --> 00:05:59,552
[SPEAKER_01]: It is... this is a form of a method as well.

99
00:06:00,072 --> 00:06:05,336
[SPEAKER_01]: But a method that you cannot observe, psychologize, measure.

100
00:06:05,497 --> 00:06:05,777
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

101
00:06:06,383 --> 00:06:07,564
[SPEAKER_00]: Or decide beforehand.

102
00:06:08,184 --> 00:06:08,804
[SPEAKER_00]: I think, yeah.

103
00:06:08,824 --> 00:06:09,545
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically...

104
00:06:10,505 --> 00:06:13,607
[SPEAKER_00]: So, is it... it's something... it's somewhere other than faith.

105
00:06:15,948 --> 00:06:18,789
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not to say that faith is necessarily a bad thing.

106
00:06:18,989 --> 00:06:19,570
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

107
00:06:19,810 --> 00:06:21,110
[SPEAKER_01]: But faith is there in the front.

108
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:21,611
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

109
00:06:21,911 --> 00:06:22,911
[SPEAKER_01]: You place faith in things.

110
00:06:23,171 --> 00:06:23,431
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

111
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,073
[SPEAKER_01]: In order to start practicing or whatever.

112
00:06:26,093 --> 00:06:27,293
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it is necessary in that sense.

113
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:28,454
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's... That's what we're talking about.

114
00:06:28,474 --> 00:06:29,114
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a different direction.

115
00:06:29,134 --> 00:06:30,255
[SPEAKER_00]: Faith cannot arrive at this.

116
00:06:31,473 --> 00:06:33,455
[SPEAKER_00]: So, not fake, not preference.

117
00:06:34,015 --> 00:06:34,635
[SPEAKER_01]: No preference.

118
00:06:34,755 --> 00:06:37,598
[SPEAKER_01]: I want this, I don't want that.

119
00:06:38,438 --> 00:06:43,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Tradition or from what you've heard, doing it because... Just watch your nostrils, just pay attention to that.

120
00:06:44,943 --> 00:06:47,445
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this examination of properties, breaking it down.

121
00:06:47,485 --> 00:06:50,727
[SPEAKER_01]: Analysis, apologizing, scientific pontification.

122
00:06:51,148 --> 00:06:52,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, everything is constantly changing and so on.

123
00:06:52,869 --> 00:06:54,230
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all just made up of these things.

124
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:54,590
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

125
00:06:54,610 --> 00:06:56,792
[SPEAKER_01]: Just explaining everything nicely and neatly in front.

126
00:06:58,962 --> 00:07:05,086
[SPEAKER_00]: Relying on insight from a view, that's again a speculative translation, but I say that...

127
00:07:05,106 --> 00:07:09,188
[SPEAKER_00]: I take that to mean something like... Well, that's as literal as I can get, so...

128
00:07:09,928 --> 00:07:11,689
[SPEAKER_00]: The insight from a view.

129
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:15,391
[SPEAKER_00]: Nidjana, the insight from a view, and then...

130
00:07:15,411 --> 00:07:16,752
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the result of a certain view.

131
00:07:16,772 --> 00:07:17,292
[SPEAKER_00]: So, exactly.

132
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:26,277
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I think of it as being like having some kind of understanding based upon a view, which is sort of applying to what's in front.

133
00:07:26,357 --> 00:07:27,338
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're extending

134
00:07:29,043 --> 00:07:40,449
[SPEAKER_01]: The principle that you get from your view, as in you're not seeing it directly, you just sort of... if this is the case here, so it's to this extent, because that's how you understood the case in front of you.

135
00:07:41,949 --> 00:07:52,394
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, yeah, you can be holding on to a view, and because of that not seeing your current state of the mind, because you're reinterpreting it from the point of view that you have on account of it.

136
00:07:53,755 --> 00:07:55,715
[SPEAKER_01]: Which kind of makes it, again, influence...

137
00:07:55,735 --> 00:07:57,676
[SPEAKER_00]: Applying an external template on...

138
00:07:57,796 --> 00:07:58,376
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

139
00:07:58,396 --> 00:08:02,437
[SPEAKER_01]: External template that has been created on account of some insight of some view.

140
00:08:02,837 --> 00:08:04,858
[SPEAKER_01]: Right or wrong doesn't matter.

141
00:08:04,878 --> 00:08:07,378
[SPEAKER_01]: By the way, even the right view works the same way.

142
00:08:08,298 --> 00:08:10,659
[SPEAKER_01]: You create the right template, so to speak.

143
00:08:11,299 --> 00:08:13,760
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when arahant is beyond the view, beyond the template.

144
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,160
[SPEAKER_01]: He has fulfilled the template.

145
00:08:16,334 --> 00:08:23,157
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's the Buddha's words on loving-kindness, anapagammas, dittīṃ anapagamma.

146
00:08:23,177 --> 00:08:30,160
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not having, not going into a view.

147
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:32,001
[SPEAKER_00]: Not wrong views or fixed views.

148
00:08:32,461 --> 00:08:35,102
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

149
00:08:35,582 --> 00:08:36,923
[SPEAKER_01]: Not still depending on the view.

150
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:46,990
[SPEAKER_00]: So...

151
00:08:50,812 --> 00:09:12,598
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he says... he asks the monks, he says... Bhikkhus, for a bhikkhu having... who has seen a sight with the eye, for whom there's passion, aversion, distraction internally, and who understands, for me, there is passion, aversion, distraction internally,

152
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:26,197
[SPEAKER_00]: All for a bhikkhu, having seen, who's seen a sight with the eye, for whom there isn't passion, aversion, distraction internally, who understands, for me, there isn't passion, aversion, distraction internally, bhikkhus, are these things to be known by means of faith?

153
00:09:27,598 --> 00:09:28,298
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely not.

154
00:09:28,398 --> 00:09:30,580
[SPEAKER_00]: Are they to be known by means of preference?

155
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,120
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

156
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,301
[SPEAKER_00]: Are they to be known by means of tradition?

157
00:09:33,481 --> 00:09:34,042
[SPEAKER_00]: Impossible.

158
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:36,063
[SPEAKER_01]: By an examination of properties?

159
00:09:36,163 --> 00:09:39,625
[SPEAKER_01]: It's amongst all of the, the entire domain where these, these things apply.

160
00:09:40,365 --> 00:09:41,666
[SPEAKER_01]: It can only be known directly.

161
00:09:42,441 --> 00:09:43,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Right here, right now.

162
00:09:43,362 --> 00:09:47,784
[SPEAKER_00]: So, or are they... yeah, well, no, lying on the inside from the views.

163
00:09:48,104 --> 00:09:51,546
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the monks say, no, can't take it.

164
00:09:51,566 --> 00:09:56,529
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, he says, are these things to be known having seen them with understanding?

165
00:09:57,510 --> 00:10:01,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, can't take it.

166
00:10:02,233 --> 00:10:11,078
[SPEAKER_00]: This, bhikkhus, is the method by means of which a bhikkhu, from a place other than faith, tradition, etc., might describe final knowledge.

167
00:10:13,477 --> 00:10:15,899
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the method is to know the background of your method.

168
00:10:21,262 --> 00:10:29,808
[SPEAKER_01]: Of your faith, of your observances, of your analysis, of your traditional techniques.

169
00:10:31,429 --> 00:10:33,811
[SPEAKER_01]: If you know the background of it, you're going beyond the method.

170
00:10:33,951 --> 00:10:37,093
[SPEAKER_01]: And, yeah, you can call that a right method.

171
00:10:39,034 --> 00:10:41,456
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it can only be seen

172
00:10:42,705 --> 00:10:44,371
[SPEAKER_01]: Through understanding.

173
00:10:44,471 --> 00:10:46,659
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, seeing it means understanding it.

174
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:47,281
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

175
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:51,743
[SPEAKER_00]: And understanding in the sense of... And understanding means dispassion.

176
00:10:52,464 --> 00:10:53,565
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, completely.

177
00:10:53,905 --> 00:11:00,470
[SPEAKER_00]: But understanding, not just... not just... No, understanding what exactly what it says.

178
00:11:00,791 --> 00:11:03,233
[SPEAKER_01]: Not understanding the contents of this particular thing.

179
00:11:03,253 --> 00:11:04,254
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not understanding.

180
00:11:04,314 --> 00:11:08,978
[SPEAKER_01]: That's you examining the properties and then kind of classifying and collecting them.

181
00:11:09,018 --> 00:11:09,218
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

182
00:11:09,598 --> 00:11:09,758
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

183
00:11:09,898 --> 00:11:10,719
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding what?

184
00:11:10,899 --> 00:11:15,804
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding what state of mind is simultaneously present with this simultaneously enduring sight.

185
00:11:15,944 --> 00:11:16,104
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

186
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:20,626
[SPEAKER_01]: What state of mind is simultaneously present with this simultaneously enduring feeling?

187
00:11:22,547 --> 00:11:24,208
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it the state of mind with passion?

188
00:11:24,308 --> 00:11:26,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it the state of mind free from passion?

189
00:11:26,449 --> 00:11:27,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Know that to its extent.

190
00:11:28,131 --> 00:11:32,273
[SPEAKER_01]: It means you're getting to know the nature of the phenomenon that your mind is.

191
00:11:33,674 --> 00:11:38,337
[SPEAKER_00]: And if there is passion, aversion, distraction there... You know it as such.

192
00:11:38,357 --> 00:11:40,119
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you see, so not kind of shrinking away from it.

193
00:11:40,419 --> 00:11:41,900
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, now I need to do something else.

194
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:42,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

195
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:42,740
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no.

196
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:44,682
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to know it to the extent that it is.

197
00:11:44,702 --> 00:11:44,802
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

198
00:11:45,777 --> 00:11:48,558
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the problem is not in those thoughts.

199
00:11:48,738 --> 00:11:50,819
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is not even in that mind, so to speak.

200
00:11:50,879 --> 00:11:53,259
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is you not understanding its extent.

201
00:11:53,319 --> 00:11:57,141
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you either go too close, too far, trying to overly affirm it, overly deny.

202
00:11:57,541 --> 00:11:59,861
[SPEAKER_01]: You get involved, you get burdened by the whole thing.

203
00:12:00,602 --> 00:12:02,622
[SPEAKER_01]: And then it becomes your passion, your everything.

204
00:12:02,702 --> 00:12:03,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Because why?

205
00:12:03,202 --> 00:12:04,203
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're acting out of it.

206
00:12:11,045 --> 00:12:12,625
[SPEAKER_01]: And you certainly, it's not a matter of choice.

207
00:12:13,466 --> 00:12:14,346
[SPEAKER_01]: That's another preference.

208
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:21,692
[SPEAKER_01]: To just choose to... okay, I will not have these states of mind, because they're unwholesome.

209
00:12:23,793 --> 00:12:26,754
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha asked, can you obtain these things by preference?

210
00:12:27,395 --> 00:12:27,555
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

211
00:12:28,595 --> 00:12:30,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Means you can't choose your way out of it.

212
00:12:30,596 --> 00:12:30,816
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

213
00:12:31,476 --> 00:12:40,400
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you know the state of mind within the present enduring choice, towards sight, towards feeling, towards whatever, that's how you step outside of it.

214
00:12:41,603 --> 00:12:49,027
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not something you can look at directly, which would be a matter of choice, a matter of examination.

215
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:49,748
[SPEAKER_01]: That's impossible.

216
00:12:52,369 --> 00:12:55,991
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's sort of discerning the... the proper route.

217
00:12:56,452 --> 00:13:01,014
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the proper necessary basis, which is always peripheral from where you look.

218
00:13:01,174 --> 00:13:03,095
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, because normally... That's a definition of it.

219
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:03,776
[SPEAKER_00]: ...the route would be me.

220
00:13:04,576 --> 00:13:05,598
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

221
00:13:05,738 --> 00:13:06,519
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the assuming.

222
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,002
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the default.

223
00:13:08,202 --> 00:13:11,607
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, see, the sight, sound, smell, taste, touch, it's always in front of you.

224
00:13:11,828 --> 00:13:14,472
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always the perception of it has to be in front.

225
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:16,295
[SPEAKER_00]: And this is not in front.

226
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:20,301
[SPEAKER_01]: And you could see, that's what all these things have in common.

227
00:13:20,321 --> 00:13:21,201
[SPEAKER_01]: They're also in front.

228
00:13:21,822 --> 00:13:24,443
[SPEAKER_01]: Examination, preference.

229
00:13:24,823 --> 00:13:25,584
[SPEAKER_01]: Just do this.

230
00:13:26,064 --> 00:13:32,347
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I just have clarity of information what needs to be done, told, passed down to me by tradition, by requirement, and I'll do it.

231
00:13:32,547 --> 00:13:33,408
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all in the front.

232
00:13:33,508 --> 00:13:34,948
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all where the senses are.

233
00:13:36,609 --> 00:13:41,211
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, the real method is actually completely the opposite direction, defined by what's not in front.

234
00:13:43,713 --> 00:13:45,954
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't see your mind on the level of the sight.

235
00:13:47,668 --> 00:13:49,849
[SPEAKER_01]: But the lust is not in the sight, it's in the mind.

236
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:54,853
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, all you keep doing, in order to get rid of the lust in the mind, is examining the sights.

237
00:13:55,793 --> 00:13:57,914
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why you are unsuccessful.

238
00:13:58,215 --> 00:14:02,838
[SPEAKER_01]: Manipulating, preventing, controlling, denying, indulging, all these, like, revolts against it.

239
00:14:04,493 --> 00:14:05,454
[SPEAKER_01]: Completely misplaced.

240
00:14:05,634 --> 00:14:05,834
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

241
00:14:05,974 --> 00:14:11,078
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't know that there is simultaneously a present enduring root of that significance of that whole sight.

242
00:14:11,699 --> 00:14:21,386
[SPEAKER_01]: And everything that's pressuring you, bothering you, or exciting you, whatever, whichever sight it is, the necessary root is the state of mind effectively lost, or the state of mind non-effectively lost.

243
00:14:23,188 --> 00:14:25,129
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to train that peripheral vision.

244
00:14:25,209 --> 00:14:30,834
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot, like, find a way that will then enable you to look at it directly and, okay, now I'm done.

245
00:14:40,305 --> 00:14:41,386
[SPEAKER_00]: So, pick up the sign.

246
00:14:41,886 --> 00:14:43,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Pick up the sign of your mind.

247
00:14:45,969 --> 00:14:49,272
[SPEAKER_01]: The necessary condition for the arising of right view.

248
00:14:50,453 --> 00:14:52,514
[SPEAKER_01]: Become familiar with the sign of your mind.

249
00:14:52,614 --> 00:14:55,437
[SPEAKER_01]: Sign of the phenomenon of the mind, for what it is.

250
00:14:56,457 --> 00:15:06,105
[SPEAKER_01]: See, for as long as you assume that you can observe your mind on the level of the senses, with a method of observation, means you don't know what the nature of the mind is, which means you're ignorant of its signs.

251
00:15:09,968 --> 00:15:14,989
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why always, like, when we're doing those previous interrogations, like, what is your current mood?

252
00:15:15,069 --> 00:15:15,410
[SPEAKER_01]: How you feel?

253
00:15:15,430 --> 00:15:20,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's already a background of whatever you're doing now, trying to understand now, want to say now, want to deal with it now.

254
00:15:21,451 --> 00:15:22,552
[SPEAKER_01]: You're in a certain mood.

255
00:15:22,992 --> 00:15:26,653
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you start looking for your mind, in the direction where your mood is.

256
00:15:26,733 --> 00:15:28,173
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's not something you can put in front of it.

257
00:15:28,873 --> 00:15:34,635
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you performing effort of putting something in front is on the basis of that, within that container of that mood.

258
00:15:37,018 --> 00:15:41,961
[SPEAKER_01]: The entire life of the tree is contained within the existence of the roots.

259
00:15:42,681 --> 00:15:44,222
[SPEAKER_01]: Functioning roots, present roots.

260
00:15:46,303 --> 00:15:50,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter how big the tree gets, its life is always within the basis of this.

261
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:53,868
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if that disappears, none of the extent of the tree can remain.

262
00:16:17,724 --> 00:16:21,985
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a different sutta.

263
00:16:22,465 --> 00:16:35,990
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this root of the unwholesome, Anguttara, Book of Threes, the Buddha says there are these three grounds for the arising of action.

264
00:16:37,670 --> 00:16:41,731
[SPEAKER_00]: Which three?

265
00:16:41,791 --> 00:16:46,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Lobha, so I'm going to translate as desire is the ground for the arising of action.

266
00:17:00,667 --> 00:17:02,929
[SPEAKER_00]: Aversion is a ground for the arising of action.

267
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:08,393
[SPEAKER_00]: Ignorance is a ground for the arising of action.

268
00:17:11,176 --> 00:17:15,920
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever action is done with desire, born of desire, grounded in desire, arisen out of desire,

269
00:17:17,799 --> 00:17:21,781
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever self-existence is born, there that action bears fruit.

270
00:17:23,562 --> 00:17:35,827
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever that action bears fruit, there one experiences the result of that action, either in this life, or having been reborn in some other way, or arising in some other way.

271
00:17:41,149 --> 00:17:44,431
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever action is done with aversion, whatever action is done with ignorance,

272
00:17:46,135 --> 00:17:56,700
[SPEAKER_00]: Or delusion, or distraction, or born of ignorance, grounded in ignorance, arisen out of ignorance, wherever self-existence is born, there that action ripens.

273
00:17:58,401 --> 00:18:07,105
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever that... wherever that action ripens, there one experiences the result of that action, either in this very life, or having arisen in some other way.

274
00:18:09,035 --> 00:18:26,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Suppose, bhikkhus, some seeds that were not broken, not rotten, not spoiled by wind and heat, taken from the most excellent part, well embedded, laid in the good ground, were laid in the good ground, in well-prepared earth, and the sky would provide the right amount of rain.

275
00:18:27,419 --> 00:18:31,020
[SPEAKER_00]: These seeds, bhikkhus, will undergo an increased growth abundance.

276
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,601
[SPEAKER_00]: And just this way, bhikkhus, whatever action is done with desire,

277
00:18:37,577 --> 00:18:39,980
[SPEAKER_00]: I've done with aversion, I've done with ignorance.

278
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:43,664
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever self-existence is born, there that action ripens.

279
00:18:44,284 --> 00:18:52,092
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever that action ripens, there one experiences the result of that action, either in this very life, or having loosed in some other way.

280
00:19:14,402 --> 00:19:23,005
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just these... the idea of these... the root, the necessary basis... of... of action, in this case, action.

281
00:19:44,355 --> 00:19:49,856
[SPEAKER_01]: What about... Maybe this isn't going to kind of... Well, it kind of sounds pretty much straightforward.

282
00:19:49,876 --> 00:19:50,116
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

283
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:59,278
[SPEAKER_01]: Whenever you choose to act, you will do so in regard to how you feel.

284
00:20:02,879 --> 00:20:10,561
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can... otherwise, you can say that there's... there is... for... for an unenlightened mind, there is only one basis of action.

285
00:20:11,001 --> 00:20:11,321
[SPEAKER_00]: Uh-huh.

286
00:20:12,498 --> 00:20:13,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Action by body, speech and mind.

287
00:20:13,799 --> 00:20:15,580
[SPEAKER_01]: That basis is craving towards feeling.

288
00:20:19,002 --> 00:20:20,764
[SPEAKER_00]: Which of these routes of greed?

289
00:20:20,884 --> 00:20:24,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Which can be craving through greed, craving through aversion, craving through distraction.

290
00:20:24,706 --> 00:20:30,310
[SPEAKER_00]: What it is, is basically your response to a feeling.

291
00:20:32,046 --> 00:20:34,747
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, yeah, you can respond to the feeling.

292
00:20:34,807 --> 00:20:35,467
[SPEAKER_01]: It is.

293
00:20:35,607 --> 00:20:37,107
[SPEAKER_00]: Your attitude.

294
00:20:37,447 --> 00:20:40,628
[SPEAKER_01]: Your attitude towards the feeling that you've been subjected to.

295
00:20:40,648 --> 00:20:40,948
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

296
00:20:41,228 --> 00:20:44,789
[SPEAKER_01]: Pleasant, unpleasant, or neither unpleasant or pleasant.

297
00:20:45,029 --> 00:20:56,151
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the... and that there cannot be any other action on the level of kamma that will have its ripening, as the Buddha describes it, unless it's rooted in that.

298
00:20:56,931 --> 00:21:00,432
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, if you learn how to act,

299
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:05,848
[SPEAKER_01]: Without being rooted in craving, you will be an arahant.

300
00:21:05,908 --> 00:21:13,289
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why that does not constitute the action on the level of karma and vipāka, because there is no craving.

301
00:21:14,250 --> 00:21:17,610
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not done by him, for him, for others.

302
00:21:17,950 --> 00:21:18,330
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not.

303
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:20,811
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that whole domain is gone.

304
00:21:21,431 --> 00:21:25,812
[SPEAKER_01]: Domain that's been existing on account of greed, aversion, delusion being there.

305
00:21:26,612 --> 00:21:29,013
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's the second part of the synthesis.

306
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:30,373
[SPEAKER_00]: It's these three grounds.

307
00:21:31,548 --> 00:21:32,528
[SPEAKER_00]: The arising of action.

308
00:21:33,769 --> 00:21:34,349
[SPEAKER_00]: Which three?

309
00:21:34,449 --> 00:21:35,029
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-desire.

310
00:21:35,289 --> 00:21:35,970
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-desire.

311
00:21:36,230 --> 00:21:36,890
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-aversion.

312
00:21:36,950 --> 00:21:37,570
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-aversion.

313
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,271
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-influence.

314
00:21:38,371 --> 00:21:38,531
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

315
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:53,777
[SPEAKER_00]: Whenever an action... whatever action is done with non-desire, born of non-desire, grown up in non-desire, arisen out of non-desire, being without desire, in this way, that action is abandoned, put off at the root, made like a construct.

316
00:21:53,797 --> 00:21:59,179
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever action is done without craving, it's not an action anymore.

317
00:21:59,299 --> 00:21:59,559
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

318
00:22:00,911 --> 00:22:01,932
[SPEAKER_01]: The action is abundant.

319
00:22:03,693 --> 00:22:07,335
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's internal state of mind determines whether you act or not.

320
00:22:07,435 --> 00:22:09,276
[SPEAKER_01]: Not what you do externally.

321
00:22:09,577 --> 00:22:11,938
[SPEAKER_01]: It can be then observed by others.

322
00:22:12,018 --> 00:22:15,821
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, there are certain things that you cannot do once the craving is gone.

323
00:22:15,841 --> 00:22:20,464
[SPEAKER_01]: Have sexual intercourse, intentionally kill somebody, lie and things like that.

324
00:22:21,264 --> 00:22:22,005
[SPEAKER_01]: But, eh...

325
00:22:22,752 --> 00:22:25,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Many other things can be done by both.

326
00:22:25,814 --> 00:22:27,156
[SPEAKER_01]: By an arahant and by a pūtujana.

327
00:22:27,256 --> 00:22:30,878
[SPEAKER_01]: They can both eat, they both walk, talk, choose, prefer.

328
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:33,220
[SPEAKER_01]: But one is action, the other one isn't.

329
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:39,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Because one is rooted in craving how he feels at the time, the other one is not rooted in that, because he doesn't feel anything anymore.

330
00:22:39,925 --> 00:22:43,068
[SPEAKER_00]: So the roots of the action for the arahant is non-desire.

331
00:22:44,688 --> 00:22:45,488
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, yeah, yeah.

332
00:22:46,208 --> 00:22:47,629
[SPEAKER_01]: The necessary basis for...

333
00:22:48,249 --> 00:22:50,009
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not really action, yeah.

334
00:22:50,029 --> 00:22:51,330
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

335
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:57,211
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, if you decide to call it an action, sure, but then you need to understand it's not the action of Patujana.

336
00:22:57,491 --> 00:23:05,213
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not the same action of Patujana, because as the Buddha describes, one results in this whole mess of suffering right now, or even later, or both.

337
00:23:05,733 --> 00:23:09,714
[SPEAKER_01]: The other one is cut off its root right there and then, because he hasn't been done by clarity.

338
00:23:09,734 --> 00:23:12,855
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no vipaka, there's no result from this, so it's not really an action.

339
00:23:12,935 --> 00:23:14,195
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not an action, exactly.

340
00:23:15,155 --> 00:23:15,736
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean.

341
00:23:15,756 --> 00:23:23,842
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if you were to learn how can you act without needing to crave and desire the action, you'll be an arahant.

342
00:23:24,723 --> 00:23:25,944
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you'll be at least a sotāpanna.

343
00:23:26,384 --> 00:23:29,767
[SPEAKER_01]: If you then develop that type of action, you will be an arahant.

344
00:23:31,412 --> 00:23:32,493
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what we spoke before.

345
00:23:32,513 --> 00:23:36,275
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you know, see, you think you act only when you're kind of aware of what you want to do.

346
00:23:36,355 --> 00:23:40,897
[SPEAKER_01]: But even now, while we're talking, my hands are moving, my feet change position.

347
00:23:41,457 --> 00:23:42,018
[SPEAKER_01]: All of these things.

348
00:23:42,038 --> 00:23:45,920
[SPEAKER_01]: So the body keeps acting in its own domain, in its own regard.

349
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:52,263
[SPEAKER_01]: But you regard that as secondary to my action that I choose to voluntarily, volitionally perform.

350
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:53,644
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the other way around.

351
00:23:54,244 --> 00:24:00,788
[SPEAKER_01]: The only reason you can choose and perform things with extra layer of volition is because the body allows you to.

352
00:24:01,469 --> 00:24:09,314
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means the domain of this random movements of the body, breathing, shifting, changing postures, standing up, going to the toilet, eating, all of that, that is on its own.

353
00:24:09,494 --> 00:24:12,477
[SPEAKER_01]: And those are already actions that don't require craving to be done.

354
00:24:13,137 --> 00:24:15,939
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're all right... all you're doing when you're...

355
00:24:16,059 --> 00:24:18,160
[SPEAKER_00]: Intentionally, I'm going to put my hand in the air now.

356
00:24:18,601 --> 00:24:23,144
[SPEAKER_00]: You're basically bringing awareness to this whole domain of stuff that's there anyway.

357
00:24:23,304 --> 00:24:24,785
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

358
00:24:24,805 --> 00:24:26,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you're not the creator of any of that.

359
00:24:26,786 --> 00:24:26,986
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

360
00:24:28,668 --> 00:24:29,348
[SPEAKER_01]: You're within it.

361
00:24:29,698 --> 00:24:29,918
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

362
00:24:29,958 --> 00:24:34,060
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your volition is secondary to the domain where you can exercise it.

363
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:34,440
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

364
00:24:35,601 --> 00:24:43,564
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's usually my volition is the center of the action and these are all its results and repercussions.

365
00:24:43,584 --> 00:24:48,266
[SPEAKER_00]: So, rooting all of those actions that are going on already.

366
00:24:49,587 --> 00:24:49,747
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

367
00:24:49,867 --> 00:24:50,887
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's that's that's the point.

368
00:24:50,907 --> 00:24:56,290
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, see, people don't... if people can't differentiate this, that's when you start to blame everything and nothing.

369
00:24:56,510 --> 00:24:56,850
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

370
00:24:57,497 --> 00:25:02,821
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I need to move, I can't move my leg, I can't do this, I can't do that, because that's craving, that's craving, that's craving.

371
00:25:02,841 --> 00:25:03,782
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't have this, I can't have that.

372
00:25:03,802 --> 00:25:05,023
[SPEAKER_00]: But that in itself, that response is an action.

373
00:25:05,043 --> 00:25:06,624
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already something you fully do it.

374
00:25:06,644 --> 00:25:07,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

375
00:25:07,264 --> 00:25:08,465
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's more like... No, no, no.

376
00:25:08,485 --> 00:25:09,226
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all the way around.

377
00:25:09,306 --> 00:25:11,747
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all these things are done, they don't need the craving.

378
00:25:12,048 --> 00:25:12,228
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

379
00:25:12,248 --> 00:25:16,071
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let me just make a point then, when I'm aware that I'm acting out of craving, not do that.

380
00:25:16,171 --> 00:25:16,471
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

381
00:25:25,355 --> 00:25:27,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, if you accidentally kill somebody, it's not a murder.

382
00:25:28,996 --> 00:25:29,696
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an accident.

383
00:25:29,956 --> 00:25:33,797
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what I'm referring to is, like, volitionally performing these actions.

384
00:25:34,337 --> 00:25:34,818
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why...

385
00:25:34,878 --> 00:25:41,279
[SPEAKER_01]: It requires this kind of... a certain perpetuation of the level of craving, desire for action.

386
00:25:41,439 --> 00:25:41,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

387
00:25:42,420 --> 00:25:45,520
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the extent of it cannot be done by an arahant.

388
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:47,841
[SPEAKER_01]: He doesn't have that at all.

389
00:25:47,861 --> 00:25:51,322
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it talks about greed, aversion, destruction.

390
00:25:52,352 --> 00:25:55,396
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like a non-greed, non-aversion, non-distraction.

391
00:25:55,476 --> 00:25:57,959
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's simply restraint.

392
00:25:59,340 --> 00:25:59,761
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

393
00:25:59,841 --> 00:26:00,602
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the starting point.

394
00:26:00,742 --> 00:26:02,524
[SPEAKER_01]: And see, there's another interesting thing here.

395
00:26:03,105 --> 00:26:07,590
[SPEAKER_01]: It's that Kaya said, by not understanding this, you put your volition first.

396
00:26:07,830 --> 00:26:08,010
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

397
00:26:08,050 --> 00:26:09,572
[SPEAKER_01]: You think that's the root.

398
00:26:11,194 --> 00:26:11,534
[SPEAKER_01]: And then...

399
00:26:13,539 --> 00:26:17,442
[SPEAKER_01]: You try to sort of even practice the dhamma through that.

400
00:26:18,282 --> 00:26:25,147
[SPEAKER_01]: And by that, I mean, you become aware that the body has its own domain where it does all these things.

401
00:26:25,207 --> 00:26:29,470
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't need to keep thinking about all these little movements, postures, scratching.

402
00:26:30,471 --> 00:26:33,714
[SPEAKER_01]: But now you realize, but I must be aware of everything.

403
00:26:34,234 --> 00:26:44,583
[SPEAKER_01]: So, but instead of seeing that your volition is secondary, and by understanding the right order, you become aware of it, you try to then sort of subjugate everything to your volition.

404
00:26:44,623 --> 00:26:50,909
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when you get the vipassana techniques of, oh, I can't just be aware of my obvious desires and cravings.

405
00:26:51,049 --> 00:26:53,271
[SPEAKER_01]: I must be volitionally aware of

406
00:26:53,731 --> 00:26:57,734
[SPEAKER_01]: Sitting, sitting, moving, talking, touching, touching, leaving...

407
00:26:57,754 --> 00:26:58,314
[SPEAKER_01]: Ridiculous.

408
00:26:58,454 --> 00:26:59,155
[SPEAKER_00]: So, not just...

409
00:26:59,295 --> 00:27:02,337
[SPEAKER_00]: I shouldn't just be aware of the fact that I'm walking, but rising...

410
00:27:02,397 --> 00:27:03,778
[SPEAKER_01]: I must keep bringing my volition.

411
00:27:03,878 --> 00:27:05,299
[SPEAKER_01]: Bring volition, bring volition.

412
00:27:05,359 --> 00:27:06,980
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I missed a bit then.

413
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:07,860
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

414
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:14,084
[SPEAKER_01]: Failing to see that what you're doing is actually trying to force practice of dhamma through the wrong order.

415
00:27:14,144 --> 00:27:14,785
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

416
00:27:15,325 --> 00:27:16,426
[SPEAKER_00]: You're trying to put yourself first.

417
00:27:16,486 --> 00:27:22,870
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it doesn't matter how much volitionally you commit to it, you're committing to your wrong view of what comes first.

418
00:27:23,457 --> 00:27:23,637
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

419
00:27:24,458 --> 00:27:33,464
[SPEAKER_01]: But instead, you need to recognize that all this lifting, putting, sitting, persisting, scratching, is done by the body on that level.

420
00:27:33,504 --> 00:27:35,466
[SPEAKER_01]: So just don't lose the corner of your eye.

421
00:27:35,486 --> 00:27:36,847
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't need to attend to it.

422
00:27:37,587 --> 00:27:38,308
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the whole point.

423
00:27:38,708 --> 00:27:45,853
[SPEAKER_01]: By becoming familiar with the actions that don't need your attending, your volition, you're becoming familiar with the actions that don't require craving.

424
00:27:46,694 --> 00:27:47,595
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you can relax.

425
00:27:47,835 --> 00:27:48,095
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

426
00:27:48,901 --> 00:27:52,485
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, all I need to do is stay at the gate in case the craving comes.

427
00:27:52,625 --> 00:27:53,667
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's not, I have no...

428
00:27:53,727 --> 00:27:55,248
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to stop and search everyone.

429
00:27:56,025 --> 00:27:56,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's not the point.

430
00:27:56,786 --> 00:28:02,990
[SPEAKER_01]: The point is, I know where the craving is there, when the aversion is there, when the desire for distraction is there.

431
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:05,091
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I don't act out of.

432
00:28:05,451 --> 00:28:10,235
[SPEAKER_01]: And that is always, as I said before in previous talks, that is always intentional.

433
00:28:10,715 --> 00:28:13,517
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot unintentionally choose a desire.

434
00:28:14,157 --> 00:28:21,242
[SPEAKER_01]: It always implies awareness of that choice, which means you're always responsible for choosing desire, aversion and distraction.

435
00:28:22,623 --> 00:28:36,476
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of trying to override everything with your completely misconceived volition, you have to start including the volition as secondary to all these little things that you actually do throughout the day, and you just need to remain aware of them peripherally.

436
00:28:36,656 --> 00:28:42,081
[SPEAKER_01]: Just know that it's being done, not specifically to what extent and how fast I'm moving my leg.

437
00:28:43,919 --> 00:28:48,082
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the body postures are the general reference points.

438
00:28:48,423 --> 00:28:53,887
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter what I do now, as long as I keep a corner of the eye that this body, this lump of flesh is seated.

439
00:28:55,188 --> 00:28:57,610
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever is done, has to be done within that posture.

440
00:28:59,512 --> 00:29:01,633
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, I have a choice to get up, to change the posture.

441
00:29:01,733 --> 00:29:02,874
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a volitional choice.

442
00:29:03,675 --> 00:29:06,017
[SPEAKER_01]: But even that can eventually become normal.

443
00:29:06,157 --> 00:29:07,258
[SPEAKER_01]: There's a need to stand up.

444
00:29:07,338 --> 00:29:07,878
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll stand up.

445
00:29:08,039 --> 00:29:09,560
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to always attend to it.

446
00:29:11,119 --> 00:29:16,663
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead of trying to override everything with your volition, start including, basically, your volition as second to everything.

447
00:29:18,564 --> 00:29:25,189
[SPEAKER_01]: The only reason you can choose, you can will things, is because there is a body, in its own domain, performing all these things anyway, anyhow.

448
00:29:26,390 --> 00:29:36,697
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you add an extra layer of, I want this, I want that, and that extra layer is completely gratuitously rooted in desire, aversion and distraction, which you then take to become first, which you put first.

449
00:29:37,017 --> 00:29:39,419
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is no beginning, eh...

450
00:29:41,584 --> 00:29:46,485
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, this cannot be first.

451
00:29:46,545 --> 00:29:47,546
[SPEAKER_01]: It shouldn't be first.

452
00:29:48,126 --> 00:29:53,348
[SPEAKER_01]: Not knowing that, you put it first, and there is no first point when that mistake manifests there.

453
00:29:54,288 --> 00:29:55,389
[SPEAKER_01]: That is your starting point.

454
00:29:55,409 --> 00:29:58,910
[SPEAKER_01]: That is your resistance, which is why it's irreversible, once you undo it.

455
00:29:59,950 --> 00:30:01,251
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you become an arahant, you cannot

456
00:30:02,384 --> 00:30:08,371
[SPEAKER_01]: Reverse the picture and go back to the order of kutujana, because it's impossible for that order to be.

457
00:30:09,232 --> 00:30:10,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, knowing that, that's how you place it.

458
00:30:14,598 --> 00:30:15,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Turns out, we have a lot to say about it.

